        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kazuo Ishiguro\n- Works: Never Let Me Go, The Remains of the Day\n- Awards: Booker Prize, Man Booker Prize for Fiction, Arthur C. Clarke Award, National Book Critics Circle Award\n- Topics: dystopian science fiction novels\n\nFacts:\n- In 1989, Kazuo Ishiguro published The Remains of the Day, a novel.\n- In 1989, The Remains of the Day won the Man Booker Prize for Fiction.\n- In 2005, Kazuo Ishiguro published Never Let Me Go, a dystopian science fiction novel.\n- In 2005, Never Let Me Go was shortlisted for the Booker Prize and the National Book Critics Circle Award.\n- In 2006, Never Let Me Go was shortlisted for the Arthur C. Clarke Award.\n- Kazuo Ishiguro is a Japanese-born British author.",
